Same Golden Thread, different substrate.

Which leads to perhaps the strongest “summon” from your whole message:

Substrate Escape

When we identify an apparently essential property of a phenomenon, deliberately remove its familiar substrate and attempt to reconstruct the operator elsewhere.

Life without light.
Perception without eyes.
Thought without words.
Memory without brains.
Computation without silicon.
Coordination without central control.
Evolution without organisms.
Communication without explicit messages.

Some will fail. The failures tell us which features were actually essential.

And that is where Goldilocks + Golden Thread + Rumpelstiltskin + Summon all lock together:

observe → name → strip substrate → extract invariant → independently regenerate → choose the necessary amount of structure → instantiate elsewhere → measure whether it survives

That is not merely analogy-making anymore.

It is a method for discovering which parts of reality are implementations and which parts are operators.